+ * SteamARM: X keycodes as Xorg gives them with evdev -- the Linux key code
+ * (linux/input-event-codes.h) plus 8 -- instead of XQuartz's macOS virtual
+ * key code plus 8. Linux programs assume the former: Weston's X11 backend
+ * passes keycode - 8 on as a Linux key code (to Android's EventHub, through
+ * hwcomposer.waydroid, where the A key, macOS code 0, was no key at all),
+ * Chromium and Electron map keycodes to KeyboardEvent.code with an evdev
+ * table, and the default XKB keycodes (rules "base") are evdev's. The
+ * keysyms still come from the macOS layout key by key, so what each key
+ * types is unchanged. Apple's ISO keyboards swap the codes of the key left
+ * of 1 and the key right of left shift (Chromium swaps them back the same
